==============================================================================
(1/15)(2 pi a0[A])^5 / t_au = 1.119950e+18   (printed 1.11995e18, ratio 1.000000026)
(1/75) variant             = 2.239900e+17   (ratio to (1/15) form 0.200000 = 1/5 exactly)
  a Q from the (1/75) convention is sqrt(5) = 2.236068 larger
D_3/2: Q = 7.939(0.037) a.u., lambda_vac = 7325.91 A, 2j_v+1 = 4: A = 0.836301 s^-1, tau = 1195.7 ms, 2 dQ/Q -> +-11.1 ms
D_5/2: Q = 9.74(0.047) a.u., lambda_vac = 7293.48 A, 2j_v+1 = 6: A = 0.858008 s^-1, tau = 1165.5 ms, 2 dQ/Q -> +-11.2 ms
theory ratio tau(D_3/2)/tau(D_5/2) = A(D_5/2)/A(D_3/2) = 1.025957  (paper 1.0259(9))
experimental ratio 1176/1168 = 1.006849 +- 0.0122
single-channel justification: A(E2, D_3/2) / A_M1 = 1.1317e+10 (10.1 orders)
measured decay constants: Gamma(D_5/2) = 0.85616 s^-1 (0.1363 Hz), Gamma(D_3/2) = 0.85034 s^-1 (0.1353 Hz)

