4. Reshelving offset and the lifetime-fit bias (Kreuter Eqs. 2-3)
==============================================================================
Gamma' = Gamma + R = 0.859164 s^-1 (FASTER than Gamma = 0.856164); offset B = R/Gamma' = 3.49176e-03
binomially weighted fit on the same grid: T = 1182.1 ms, T - tau = +14.1 ms (the brief quotes +10 ms; the magnitude depends on the weighting and on the actual waiting times, the sign does not)
plain-exponential fit exp(-t/T) to A e^{-Gamma' t} + B on a 25 ms-5 s grid: T = 1175.1 ms, T - tau = +7.1 ms (sign is the point; magnitude is grid- and statistics-dependent, the source quotes -3 ms as its budget entry)

