6. Uys dissipator: three collapse operators and the Gamma_el/4 prefactor
==============================================================================
d rho_uu/dt = -0.020000   (-Gamma_ud rho_uu + Gamma_du rho_dd = -0.020000)
d rho_ud/dt = -0.250000-0.125000j   (-(1/2)(Gamma_Ram + Gamma_el) rho_ud = -0.250000-0.125000j)
trace derivative = +0.000e+00

Rayleigh only, c = (1/2) sqrt(Gamma_el) sigma_z: fitted coherence decay rate = 0.849999 (Gamma_el/2 = 0.850000); population drift max = 0.00e+00
NEGATIVE TEST, c = sqrt(Gamma_el/2) sigma_z: decay rate = 1.699996 = 2.0x too fast - the Gamma_el/4 dissipator prefactor is correct and must not be 'fixed'
spin-echo readout rho_uu = (1/2)(1 - e^{-(Gamma_Ram+Gamma_el) tau/2}): initial slope = 0.625000 = (Gamma_Ram+Gamma_el)/4 = 0.625000; twice it is the paper's total decoherence rate 1.250000
rejected diagnostic Gamma_el,diff = 2(Guu-Gdd)^2/(Guu+Gdd) at Guu = Gdd = 1: 0.000 (identically zero by construction, which is the ~5x underprediction the source reports)

